# Security checklist for waynesutton.ai

Convex backend, React + Vite frontend, Convex self-hosting for static assets,
Convex Auth with GitHub OAuth for the dashboard. Every public HTTP route and
public mutation is rate limited with `@convex-dev/rate-limiter`
(`convex/rateLimits.ts`). Last full audit: September 2026
(`prds/site-audit-2026-09.md`).

## Trust tiers

| Tier | Who | How it is enforced |
|------|-----|--------------------|
| Anonymous reader | Anyone | Public queries filter `published` and `unlisted`; public mutations are rate limited |
| Signed-in GitHub user | Any GitHub account | `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` non-null. Unlocks Ask AI and post AI chat only, both per-user rate limited |
| Dashboard admin | `dashboardAdmins` row, or the `DASHBOARD_PRIMARY_ADMIN_EMAIL` match in strict mode | `requireDashboardAdmin(ctx)` from `convex/dashboardAuth.ts`, checked inside every admin handler |
| CLI sync | `npm run sync`, `npm run sync:prod` | `assertSyncCaller` in `convex/lib/syncAuth.ts`: admin session, or `syncSecret` matching the `SYNC_SECRET` env var, or open when that var is unset |
| Agent pipeline | `x-api-key` on `/api/v1/drafts` and `/mcp create_draft` | Hashed pipeline keys, constant-time compare, created in the dashboard API Keys section |
| Webhooks | AgentMail, GitHub | Svix signature and `X-Hub-Signature-256` verified before the rate limit is consumed |

Per-handler auth checks are intentional. Do not move them into a wrapper.

## Secrets

- Every secret comparison goes through `secretEquals` in `convex/lib/secretCompare.ts`.
  Never compare API keys, tokens, or bootstrap keys with `===`.
- Raw vendor keys (OpenAI, Anthropic, AgentMail, R2, X) are only returned by
  `internalQuery` functions. Public `vendorKeyStatus` style queries return booleans.
- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local` are gitignored. Never commit them.
- Never schedule or call `api.*` from server code. Use `internal.*` or `components.*`.

## Env vars that gate behavior

| Variable | Effect when set |
|----------|-----------------|
| `DASHBOARD_PRIMARY_ADMIN_EMAIL` | Strict mode: that email is the only admin, `dashboardAdmins` is ignored |
| `DASHBOARD_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_KEY` | Required by `bootstrapDashboardAdmin` and `listAuthUsersForBootstrap`; also closes the open first-admin path in `grantDashboardAdmin` |
| `SYNC_SECRET` | Locks `syncPostsPublic`, `syncPagesPublic`, and the embeddings mutations to callers who pass the same value |
| `MCP_API_KEY` | Requires a Bearer token on `/mcp`. Unset means `/mcp` is public (rate limited, `create_draft` still needs a pipeline key) |
| `SITE_URL` | Origin for unsubscribe links, sitemap, RSS, OG tags. Newsletter delivery refuses non-https values |

## Intentionally public surfaces

| Surface | Bound |
|---------|-------|
| Content queries, `/api/*`, `/raw/*`, `/rss*.xml`, `/sitemap.xml`, `/llms*.txt`, `/agents.md` | Published, non-unlisted rows only; rate limited |
| `/vfs/tree`, `/vfs/exec` | Allowlisted commands, no shell, rate limited |
| `stats.heartbeat`, `stats.recordPageView` | Per-session rate limit plus dedup windows; event records, never counters |
| `newsletter.subscribe`, `contact.submitContact` | 5 per minute each |
| `newsletter.unsubscribe` | Token gated, constant-time compare |
| `demo.*` CRUD and `demo.listAll*` | Only `source: "demo"` rows are writable; lists hide non-demo unpublished rows; 30 writes per minute, 50 rows per table, 30 minute cleanup |
| `siteConfigData.getOverrides` | Runtime UI config only. Never store a secret in overrides |

## Output escaping

- HTML in `convex/http.ts`: `escapeHtml` on every interpolated value, including URLs in
  `content="..."` attributes.
- RSS: `escapeXml` for text nodes, `cdata()` for post bodies (splits `]]>`).
- Markdown rendering in the browser: `rehype-raw` followed by `rehype-sanitize`.
  `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` is admin-only (rich text editor).
- Embeds: `src/utils/embedMarkdown.ts` allowlists X and YouTube hosts only.
- External links: `target="_blank"` always pairs with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.

## Before shipping a change

- [ ] New public mutation: rate limit added in `convex/rateLimits.ts` and applied with `{ throws: true }`
- [ ] New admin function: `requireDashboardAdmin(ctx)` (or `requireDashboardAdminAction`) is the first await
- [ ] New HTTP route: rate limited, output escaped, CORS only where the route is meant to be public
- [ ] New secret: read from env or `internal` vendor key resolver, compared with `secretEquals`
- [ ] New list query: filtered by `published` (and `unlisted`) unless admin gated, bounded with `.take` or pagination
- [ ] No `Date.now()` inside queries; pass `now` from the client
- [ ] `npx convex-doctor@latest` still reports 100/100
- [ ] `npm audit` shows no new high or critical findings

## Reviewed and accepted

- Any GitHub account can sign in. Sign-in alone grants Ask AI and post AI chat, both
  per-user rate limited. It does not grant dashboard access.
- `/mcp` without `MCP_API_KEY` exposes read tools including `export_all`. Set the key
  in production if that surface should be private.
- SVG uploads are admin-only and served from the storage origin, not the site origin.
- `posts.incrementViewCount` and the `viewCounts` table are unused by the frontend.
  Remove in a later pass rather than harden.
